<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Battle of Dongola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">652</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Siege of Old Dongola, Siege of Dongola (652)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Battle of Dongola was the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-dongola">Old Dongola</a>, capital of the Nubian kingdom of Makuria, by the Arab army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-ibn-sad-ibn-abi-sarh">Abdallah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh</a>, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, in 652. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> bombarded the city with a catapult and damaged its church, but Nubian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a> inflicted heavy losses and the city held. The siege ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baqt">Baqt treaty</a>, which left Makuria independent for six centuries.</p></div>
